{"content": "1|//! Windows Hello biometric unlock support.
2|//!
3|//! Security model: biometrics are a CONVENIENCE unlock, not a replacement for the
4|//! master password. We store a random 32-byte "biometric KEK" in the OS credential
5|//! store (Windows Credential Manager via the `keyring` crate). The vault's keyfile
6|//! holds the DEK wrapped by that KEK. To release/use it we first require a genuine
7|//! Windows Hello gesture (`UserConsentVerifier`). If Hello is unavailable, disabled,
8|//! or the stored key is missing, the caller falls back to password / recovery key.
9|//!
10|//! The user's biometric data never reaches ROVault — Windows performs the check and
11|//! only tells us pass/fail.
12|
13|const SERVICE: &str = "ROVault";
14|
15|fn entry_key(vault_id: &str) -> String {
16|    format!("biometric-kek::{vault_id}")
